{
  "requirement": "`trust_but_verify::outline::OutlineContent` implements\n`trust_but_verify::NodeContents`, making it usable directly as\n`Domain::NodeContent` under\n{cite}`requirements.sdk.graph.node_content`.\n\nIts `fingerprint()` returns the selected item's retained structural hash and\nscheme under {cite}`requirements.sdk.graph.node_content.fingerprint`.\nIts `format()` returns the selected source text with recognized credentials\nredacted under {cite}`requirements.sdk.sources.redaction` and\n{cite}`requirements.sdk.graph.node_content.format`.\nBoth operations describe the source snapshot retained by the value.\n`text()` retains the original selected bytes for source inspection.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "I found no test-adequacy gap for `requirements.sdk.outlines.node_contents`. Two marked tests in `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/outline_content.rs` cover its obligations.\n\n**Obligations and the tests that cover them**\n\n1. **`OutlineContent` implements `NodeContents`.**\n   - The implementation is `impl NodeContents for OutlineContent` in `src/outline/contents.rs`. It provides only the trait methods `fingerprint` and `format`.\n   - Both tests import `NodeContents` and call these trait methods. If the impl were missing, they would not compile.\n\n2. **`fingerprint()` returns the item's retained structural hash and scheme.**\n   - `selected_contents_outlive_handles_and_later_file_edits` asserts `selected.structural_hash() == selected.fingerprint().value`.\n   - It also asserts `selected.fingerprint_scheme() == selected.fingerprint().scheme`.\n   - The scheme and hash are separate inputs, so both parts of the `Fingerprint` are checked.\n\n3. **`format()` returns the selected text with credentials redacted.**\n   - `selected_contents_outlive_handles_and_later_file_edits` asserts `selected.format()` equals `\"second\"` for a selected item.\n   - `formatted_contents_redact_credentials_while_retaining_raw_text_and_spans` uses a GitHub-token-shaped string. It asserts:\n     - the formatted text contains `[REDACTED:GitHub Token]`;\n     - the formatted text does not contain the token;\n     - the formatted text has the same line count as the source (line breaks preserved).\n   - The same test selects a sub-item (`outline().items[1]`) and checks that its `format()` is redacted while its `text()` still contains the token. This covers redaction on a selected node, not only the root.\n\n4. **Redaction does not change the structural fingerprint.** The redaction test builds two sources that differ only in the credential value and asserts their `fingerprint()` values are equal (`contents.fingerprint() == changed.fingerprint()`).\n\n5. **Both operations describe the retained snapshot.**\n   - The first test records `original = selected.fingerprint()`, drops the file handle, and overwrites the file on disk.\n   - It then asserts the fingerprint is unchanged, `format()` and `text()` are still `\"second\"`, and `from_id` now errors.\n   - A retained root selected from the value still yields the original full text. This rules out re-reading the file.\n\n6. **`text()` retains the original bytes.** The redaction test asserts `contents.text() == source` (the raw credential is kept). It also asserts that a selected item's `text()` contains the token.\n\n**Delegated obligations.** The requirements `requirements.sdk.graph.node_content`, `requirements.sdk.graph.node_content.fingerprint`, `requirements.sdk.graph.node_content.format` and `requirements.sdk.sources.redaction` are cited context. I did not reassess their own tests or implementations.\n\n**Other checks.** I found no relevant unmarked test and no conditional behavior left untested. There are no `{fixme}` acknowledgments, and none are needed.",
